id: pm-web-7kuv
title: Preview access losses before changing project shares
description: "Show caller-visible active context packets, pending decisions and agent operations that lose access under an explicitly proposed existing user or group share role/scope change. Overlap recheck: CLI public contracts and authorization/governance exports describe support/policy, not ACL consequences; pm-web Contract Explorer is operation support, Agent Context owns consented packets, Decision Inbox owns pending decisions, and swarm owns execution. Reuse these SDK and web authorization paths. No hosted configuration changes."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-28T21:58:56.592Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-28T22:40:45.966Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: View-only users cannot inspect broader scopes; preview changes no roles or packets; separately authorized changes invalidate exact affected views; unknown capabilities stay disabled. Typed SDK and CLI with bounded TOON/JSON and typed remedies; docs/example; no-git real-data evidence; seeded property and boundary validation; unchanged npm and Bun CI release gates.
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-28T21:59:47.520Z",codex-agent,"Overlap checked against current CLI public SDK declarations, fleet sources, open upstream permission-preview search (related identity/authority issue 1360), web Contract Explorer, Agent Context and Decision Inbox. No duplicate consequence preview found. Plan: read-only existing-share proposals for view/edit/none; evaluate effective direct/group access through the same query as live authorization; intersect packet audience with caller consent; reuse SDK inbox and contracts; do not execute unknown provider operations. Existing sharing remains separately authorized. No import, export, sync, durable plan, checkpoint or outbox is introduced. Test with non-git trackers, seeded ACL sequences, packet revisions, replay, extreme boundary inputs and actual share changes."
  "2026-10-28T22:17:03.472Z",codex-agent,"Implemented owner-only observational share replacement previews with the same effective owner/direct/group resolver as live access. Packet counts intersect caller consent before projection; decisions reuse the SDK-backed inbox; known core operation support reuses SDK contracts with extensions disabled. No role, packet, item, journal or configuration mutation exists. Initial boundary suite 3/3 and service-worker suite combined 31/31 pass; 500 seeded ACL/replay/audience sequences passed, plus no-git real HTTP native CLI acceptance. Three focused HTTP tests pass after excluding preview POSTs from idempotency persistence. Public immutable main copy measured 189 items, 409 unchanged source files, zero packets/requests, 31 mutation capabilities lost on downgrade and 84 total on removal; first 20 identities occupy 1513 JSON bytes. Browser desktop 1440/mobile 390 preview parity and cancel preservation pass, and real downgrade clears stale decision controls. Full gates delegated to CI as requested."
  "2026-10-28T22:20:08.477Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: in a disposable non-git copy, disabled only the access-loss branches inside previewPermissionImpact. The focused HTTP regression failed with 0 versus expected 1 pending decision; the implementation worktree was never modified. Production implementation focused HTTP subsequently passes 3/3. Added real peer transitions at all six SQL boundaries of the read-only snapshot, and optimized group evaluations into two batched calls to the same authoritative resolver. Preview POSTs are network-only in the service worker and bypass idempotency persistence while retaining expected-account checks."
  "2026-10-28T22:32:20.008Z",codex-agent,"Linked verification passed 36/36 tests (500 seeded multi-operation sequences included) in 146140 ms using the runner --timeout 600 option; the default 120-second attempt timed out on the saturated host. Real PostgreSQL peer transitions at every one of six SQL boundaries pass, showing a coherent read-only snapshot followed by fresh authorization on retry. Existing project/sharing/idempotency tests pass 37/37. Desktop/mobile browser checks at 1440/390 verify cancellation, SDK parity and removal of both stale decision and operation controls. Typecheck, lint, zero-duplication gate and all 902 source docstrings pass. No CLI/SDK defect is needed for delivery. Preparing final PR and unchanged npm/Bun CI release gates."
  "2026-10-28T22:35:04.526Z",codex-agent,"Added custom SDK status registries spanning active, blocked and terminal roles under ambient focus; regression passes 1/1 with native state read back through the SDK. Packet retrieval, discovery and impact now call the same exported audience predicate, preventing authorization-rule drift. Final focused audience regression rerun and CI verify the shared predicate. No new persistence format or native import/export/sync path was introduced."
  "2026-10-28T22:39:00.320Z",codex-agent,"Final browser race proof passes: a delayed older edit-permission response arriving after a newer view downgrade cannot restore edit controls. Permission read generations are fenced across repeated access signals and disconnects. A disposable behavioral-revert browser run is verifying that removing this generation comparison fails the same regression. Shared audience focused tests pass 2/2. All work remains scoped to this package and synthetic/public scratch data."
  "2026-10-28T22:40:45.946Z",codex-agent,The optional UI mutation run stopped at browser workspace setup before reaching the delayed-response assertion; it is not counted as a behavioral revert proof. The actual implementation browser race check passes. The main service behavioral revert remains valid (0 versus expected 1) and the shared audience read-back tests pass 2/2. Full exact-head npm/Bun CI gates remain required; local targeted gates retain all thresholds.
